---
import ResourcePageLayout from "../../../layouts/ResourcePageLayout.astro";
---

<ResourcePageLayout
  title="Bitcoin books in Danish"
  description="The best Bitcoin books available in Danish — from beginner to advanced."
  lang="en"
>
  <section class="content-section">
    <p>
      There's an ocean of good, well-written books about Bitcoin, though the vast
      majority are in English. Below is a list of the Bitcoin books that have been
      translated into Danish. Take a look — and remember, a book about Bitcoin can
      also make a fantastic gift.
    </p>
    <p>
      Buy books in Danish at
      <strong>
        <a href="https://shop21.dk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Shop21
        </a>
      </strong>
      — with the discount code "<strong>enogtyve</strong>" you get 5% off.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you'd like inspiration for more Bitcoin books in English, you can find it
      at
      <a href="https://www.bitcoinerbooks.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <strong>Bitcoinerbooks.com</strong></a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="book-card">
    <div class="book-image">
      <img
        src="/images/content/21lektioner.png"
        alt="21 Lektioner – book cover"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="book-text">
      <h2>21 Lektioner</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>21 Lektioner</strong> – Gigi, known for being both entertaining
        and technically strong, has written a book about his journey down the
        Bitcoin rabbit hole. As the name suggests, the book contains 21 lessons he
        learned along the way. It touches on philosophy, economics, and technology,
        giving a good overview of the many layers of knowledge required to
        understand Bitcoin better. The book is written in a relaxed tone and
        doesn't go deep into the topics, instead offering an introduction to each
        of them.
      </p>
      <p>
        The book can be
        <a href="https://github.com/Shop21DK/21-Lektioner/raw/master/21%20Lektioner%20-%20latest%20version.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <strong>downloaded for free</strong></a>
        or bought in physical format at
        <a href="https://shop21.dk/vare/21-lektioner/?apply_coupon=ENOGTYVE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <strong>Shop21</strong></a>.
        With the discount code "<strong>enogtyve</strong>" you get 5% off your
        order.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="book-card reverse">
    <div class="book-text">
      <h2>Bitcoinstandarden</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Bitcoinstandarden</strong> (The Bitcoin Standard) – many consider
        this book the best way to get a solid introduction to Bitcoin.
      </p>
      <p>
        It explores the history of money, from the use of shells, beads, and salt
        to metals and banknotes. The book dives into the properties that have
        enabled Bitcoin's significant growth and examines its economic, political,
        and social consequences.
      </p>
      <p>
        Readers will gain an understanding of what sets Bitcoin apart from its more
        than 10,000 successors, and why Bitcoin is immune to imitation and external
        control.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since Saifedean Ammous published the book in 2018, it has been translated
        into 30 different languages and is recognized as an essential work for
        anyone who wants to understand Bitcoin.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can buy the book in physical format here:
        <a href="https://shop21.dk/vare/bitcoinstandarden/?apply_coupon=ENOGTYVE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <strong>Shop21</strong></a>.
        <br />
        With the discount code "<strong>enogtyve</strong>" you get 5% off your order.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="book-image">
      <img
        src="/images/content/bitcoinstandarden.png"
        alt="Bitcoinstandarden – book cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <a href="#" class="back-to-top"> ↑ Back to top </a>
</ResourcePageLayout>

<style>
  /* Content sections */
  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-light, #ccc);
  }

  .content-section p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  /* Book cards */
  .book-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.1);
    border-radius: 12px;
    transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .book-card:hover {
    border-color: rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.3);
  }

  .book-card.reverse {
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
  }

  .book-image {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .book-image img {
    max-width: 220px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }

  .book-text {
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-light, #ccc);
  }

  .book-text h2 {
    color: var(--primary, #f7931a);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md, 1rem);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm, 0.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.2);
  }

  .book-text p {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .book-text p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 567px) {
    .book-card,
    .book-card.reverse {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .book-image {
      order: -1;
    }

    .book-image img {
      max-width: 180px;
    }
  }
</style>
